# Documentation maintenance

Architecture docs under `docs/`, root `AGENTS.md`, and `.cursor/rules/` are mandatory maintenance resources.

## Same-task requirement

Whenever implementation changes architecture, workflows, schema, APIs, auth, notifications, business rules, user journeys, or folder layout, update the corresponding documentation **in the same task**. Never postpone.

## Mapping (minimum)

| Change | Docs |
|--------|------|
| System components / flows | `SYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| Technical workflows / lifecycle / voting design | `SYSTEM_DESIGN.md` |
| User journeys / QA scenarios | `USER_SCENARIOS.md` |
| Business rules | `BUSINESS_LOGIC.md` + affected `USER_SCENARIOS.md` |
| Flutter structure/patterns | `FLUTTER_ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| Backend structure/patterns | `BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| Prisma/schema | `DATABASE_ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| Endpoints/contracts | `API_CONTRACTS.md` |
| AuthN/Z | `AUTHENTICATION_AND_AUTHORIZATION.md` |
| Notifications | `NOTIFICATIONS.md` |
| Decisions | `ARCHITECTURE_DECISIONS.md` |
| Paths/folders | `PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md` |
| Product scope | `PROJECT_OVERVIEW.md` / owner-approved `PRODUCT_SCENARIOS.md` |

Update Mermaid diagrams when flows or ER relationships change.

## Reality rules

- Document **implemented** behavior only as implemented; label Partial / Missing / OPEN explicitly.
- Do not invent unresolved product decisions.
- Prefer editing affected sections over rewriting every file.
- Final task reports must include a **Documentation Updates** section.
